# A module that sends itself to another class's mixin as its file loads
# (`Widget.prepend self`, as faraday's specs prepend a stub to WebMock's) is
# used as surely as `prepend Disabling` written in Widget would be, though no
# constant names it: the edge is the reference. A receiver the index does
# not hold (`Missing::Thing`, a gem's class) still takes the module. A
# module's own `extend self` hands it to nothing. One a spec mixes in is
# used by the tests (#12).
